# Copy to .env.local and fill in as needed. Nothing here is required to run
# the app — every value has a safe fallback (mock Hermes, SQLite at
# ./data/jarvis.sqlite, providers marked offline until their key is set).

# Path to the SQLite database file. ":memory:" is useful for scratch runs.
# JARVIS_DB_PATH=./data/jarvis.sqlite

# Display name for the single local owner account (security/audit actor).
# JARVIS_OWNER_NAME=Raj

# When set, OmniRouter marks the corresponding provider "online" (presence
# only — the key is never read by application code beyond this check).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Base URL of a runtime implementing JARVIS's own bespoke Hermes contract
# (contract.ts). When unset (and HERMES_AGENT_URL below is also unset),
# missions execute against the local mock Hermes adapter (clearly labeled
# `source: "mock"`).
# HERMES_API_URL=

# A real, locally-installed Hermes Agent (github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent),
# reached through its `api_server` platform rather than the bespoke contract
# above. Takes priority over HERMES_API_URL when both are set. Enable on the
# Hermes side first:
#   hermes config set platforms.api_server.enabled true
#   hermes config set platforms.api_server.host 127.0.0.1
#   hermes config set platforms.api_server.port 8642
#   echo "API_SERVER_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)" >> "$(hermes config env-path)"
#   hermes gateway run
# HERMES_AGENT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8642
# HERMES_AGENT_API_KEY=

# Spoken passcode phrase required to run "risky" Quick Actions (currently:
# Control Computer). You say this phrase out loud, the browser transcribes
# it, and the server compares the text — this proves you know the phrase,
# not that it's specifically your voice. Unset by default: risky actions are
# simply unavailable (fail closed) until you set one.
# JARVIS_VOICE_PASSCODE=

# Spotify — powers Now Playing / Focus Music with your real playback, and
# registers the browser itself as a playable device named "JARVIS" (via the
# Web Playback SDK) so playback works even with no phone/desktop app open.
# 1. Create an app at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard (free). When
#    asked which APIs/SDKs you're using, check both "Web API" and
#    "Web Playback SDK".
# 2. In its settings, add this exact Redirect URI (must be 127.0.0.1, not
#    "localhost" — Spotify no longer accepts plain-HTTP localhost redirects):
#      http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/spotify/callback
# 3. Copy the app's Client ID and Client Secret below.
# 4. Restart the dev server, then click "Connect Spotify" in Now Playing.
# Playback CONTROL (play/pause/skip/volume, and the "JARVIS" device itself)
# requires Spotify Premium; reading what's currently playing works on any
# account. Nothing here is required — Now Playing just shows a "Connect
# Spotify" prompt until it's set.
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Only override if not running on the default port 3000:
# SPOTIFY_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/spotify/callback

# ElevenLabs — optional, upgrades the "Wake" clap-routine's spoken greeting
# (Settings > Wake) from the browser's built-in voice to a real ElevenLabs
# voice. Nothing here is required — without it, the greeting still speaks,
# just using SpeechSynthesis instead.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=
